 See special note about error handling for streams in
 [`setErrorHandler`](./Server.md#seterrorhandler).
 
+When using HTTP/2, Fastify writes large string and buffer payloads in chunks,
+because a single large write on a cancelled stream can break the whole HTTP/2
+session. Streams are piped unmodified, so if your stream emits very large
+chunks, split them into smaller ones (for example, set `highWaterMark` on
+`fs.createReadStream`).
+
